1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,872
Saturday afternoon.

2
00:00:01,922 --> 00:00:07,416
Aziz steps into a lift with his phone in his hand, and the MyID screen of the mobile bank is open.

3
00:00:07,466 --> 00:00:11,352
Between the fourth and the fifth floor, his phone loses the network.

4
00:00:11,402 --> 00:00:14,760
One second earlier, MyID finished the check of his face.

5
00:00:14,810 --> 00:00:19,640
So did the check pass, or did it vanish?

6
00:00:19,690 --> 00:00:26,864
An hour ago, Aziz said yes on the consent screen, and the platform wrote a record that permits one session at MyID.

7
00:00:26,914 --> 00:00:34,376
That one session is the story of this hour: who opens it, what comes back, and what happens when something breaks on the way.

8
00:00:34,426 --> 00:00:36,536
Go back to the moment after his yes.

9
00:00:36,586 --> 00:00:41,024
Before the MyID screen opens, the mobile bank checks the phone itself.

10
00:00:41,074 --> 00:00:44,552
It looks for root access, and for signs of an emulator.

11
00:00:44,602 --> 00:00:48,824
On such a phone, the app asks for no session and starts no MyID check.

12
00:00:48,874 --> 00:00:51,728
It shows that the check is not possible on this phone.

13
00:00:51,778 --> 00:00:57,176
This check belongs to the app, because the platform and MyID cannot see the phone itself.

14
00:00:57,226 --> 00:01:01,352
Aziz's phone is clean, so the app asks the platform for a session.

15
00:01:01,402 --> 00:01:03,176
Only the mobile bank can ask.

16
00:01:03,226 --> 00:01:07,616
The bank's team adds the MyID part to the master app, and to no other app.

17
00:01:07,666 --> 00:01:13,592
Only one app holds the camera that checks faces against state records, so only one app must be defended.

18
00:01:13,642 --> 00:01:16,976
Now the backend opens the session, not the app.

19
00:01:17,026 --> 00:01:19,592
First, the platform looks at his login.

20
00:01:19,642 --> 00:01:23,576
It must have a SIM match, like his login on Monday on the mobile network.

21
00:01:23,626 --> 00:01:30,416
Without it, the platform calls nobody, counts nothing, and asks Aziz to log in again on the mobile network.

22
00:01:30,466 --> 00:01:32,288
His login has the match.

23
00:01:32,338 --> 00:01:37,400
The platform calls MyID with the credentials of the installation, which never go to the phone.

24
00:01:37,450 --> 00:01:41,312
It sends the bank's minimum face match, a configured value.

25
00:01:41,362 --> 00:01:47,648
It gets back a session identifier, and gives the mobile bank on this same phone what it needs to start the MyID screen.

26
00:01:47,698 --> 00:01:50,816
This is the proofing session, and it is now Open.

27
00:01:50,866 --> 00:01:55,616
It belongs to one customer, one device and one purpose: the step-up.

28
00:01:55,666 --> 00:01:59,312
It lives for ten minutes, a value that MyID sets.

29
00:01:59,362 --> 00:02:03,008
While it is open, no second session can open for Aziz.

30
00:02:03,058 --> 00:02:08,048
A request from a different phone gets a no, and the same phone gets back the same open session.

31
00:02:08,098 --> 00:02:13,328
Inside the mobile bank, the MyID screen captures his document and his face.

32
00:02:13,378 --> 00:02:18,944
MyID checks that the face is live, and compares the face and the document with the state records.

33
00:02:18,994 --> 00:02:22,712
Then it gives the app one thing: a one-time result code.

34
00:02:22,762 --> 00:02:25,136
The result code is not the result.

35
00:02:25,186 --> 00:02:29,960
It is a ticket that only the platform can exchange, within five minutes, one time.

36
00:02:30,010 --> 00:02:32,504
The app sends the code to the platform.

37
00:02:32,554 --> 00:02:39,896
The platform accepts it only from the device and the customer of the session, only while the session is open, and only once.

38
00:02:39,946 --> 00:02:43,640
Then it calls MyID, exchanges the code, and gets the result.

39
00:02:43,690 --> 00:02:46,280
Now suppose the code was copied on the way.

40
00:02:46,330 --> 00:02:48,776
Someone sends it again, from a different phone.

41
00:02:48,826 --> 00:02:53,240
The platform refuses it: wrong device, or code already used.

42
00:02:53,290 --> 00:02:55,112
It writes a security event.

43
00:02:55,162 --> 00:02:59,096
And it never stores the result code, so there is nothing to steal later.

44
00:02:59,146 --> 00:03:03,200
On success, the platform checks every field before it keeps it.

45
00:03:03,250 --> 00:03:07,040
The personal identification number must have fourteen digits.

46
00:03:07,090 --> 00:03:15,584
A person below the configured minimum age stays at level one, even when MyID says success, and that attempt is not counted.

47
00:03:15,634 --> 00:03:19,424
A document with an expiry date in the past is a failure.

48
00:03:19,474 --> 00:03:24,104
A face match below the bank's minimum is a failure too: face not matched.

49
00:03:24,154 --> 00:03:26,000
Failures get plain words.

50
00:03:26,050 --> 00:03:28,928
Suppose a lamp makes a glare on his document.

51
00:03:28,978 --> 00:03:34,568
MyID gives a reason code, and the platform turns it into plain words: poor image.

52
00:03:34,618 --> 00:03:38,240
Aziz reads: try again now, without the glare.

53
00:03:38,290 --> 00:03:40,664
He never sees a code or a provider name.

54
00:03:40,714 --> 00:03:43,064
Each failure also meets the limits.

55
00:03:43,114 --> 00:03:49,616
The platform counts failed attempts for the phone number, the device, and the personal identification number when it is known.

56
00:03:49,666 --> 00:03:55,808
A failure that the person or the capture caused counts, like a poor image or a face that does not match.

57
00:03:55,858 --> 00:03:58,856
A failure that the service caused does not count.

58
00:03:58,906 --> 00:04:06,944
When MyID is down, Aziz reads that the service is temporarily not available, his level does not move, and he can try again later.

59
00:04:06,994 --> 00:04:13,112
After the first counted failure, a cool-down starts, and after the second, a second cool-down.

60
00:04:13,162 --> 00:04:16,832
At the daily cap, no attempt is possible until the next day.

61
00:04:16,882 --> 00:04:19,760
The bank configures the cap and the cool-downs.

62
00:04:19,810 --> 00:04:27,704
An operator can reset the counters, for example for a phone that two customers share, and a second operator must approve the reset.

63
00:04:27,754 --> 00:04:33,320
And each new try starts again at the consent screen, because one yes opens one session.

64
00:04:33,370 --> 00:04:35,192
Back to the lift.

65
00:04:35,242 --> 00:04:41,600
When the network comes back, the app reports that the MyID screen ended, but no code reached the platform.

66
00:04:41,650 --> 00:04:45,848
The platform asks MyID for the status of the session at once.

67
00:04:45,898 --> 00:04:50,672
A code is there, so the exchange continues, and the check did not vanish.

68
00:04:50,722 --> 00:04:56,216
If MyID were still busy, the platform would ask again after the session closes.

69
00:04:56,266 --> 00:05:01,352
If no code were there, the attempt would not count, and Aziz could start again at once.

70
00:05:01,402 --> 00:05:07,496
The result is valid, so the platform keeps his verified identity, and the session is Succeeded.

71
00:05:07,546 --> 00:05:17,504
Aziz sees his names, his date of birth, the type of his document, the last four characters of its number, and the first two and last two digits of his personal identification number.

72
00:05:17,554 --> 00:05:19,376
He confirms them.

73
00:05:19,426 --> 00:05:21,248
Now a check for you.

74
00:05:21,298 --> 00:05:28,504
In the lift, the code never reached the platform: does Aziz lose an attempt?

75
00:05:28,554 --> 00:05:36,184
No: the platform asks MyID for the status, finds the code, and continues, and with no code the attempt would not count.

76
00:05:36,234 --> 00:05:41,464
Only the mobile bank runs MyID, and only after the root and emulator check.

77
00:05:41,514 --> 00:05:45,688
The platform opens the session, with credentials that stay in the bank.

78
00:05:45,738 --> 00:05:50,560
The app carries back a one-use result code, and only the platform exchanges it.

79
00:05:50,610 --> 00:05:56,080
Every failure has plain words and a counting rule, and the bank configures the limits.

80
00:05:56,130 --> 00:05:59,944
Aziz has confirmed his data, but he is not at level two yet.

81
00:05:59,994 --> 00:06:04,696
One step is left: the phone check, and the money for his mother still waits.

82
00:06:04,746 --> 00:06:09,184
Lesson 14 first shows how the platform keeps his verified identity.
